%% apiFlow_DisplayForm8825.mmdc
%% Scenario: User starts the LLC Editor app, navigates to the Form 8825
%% view, and the FILL.pdf is rendered in an iframe.
%%
%% Shows the main functions called within each service layer from
%% entry to exit (per Francisco's request).  Format follows the
%% docs/apiFlow.mmdc template.
%%
%% Ambiguities / suggestions / insights:
%%   • [Q1] Form 8825's FILL.pdf is produced by the BookToIRS pipeline
%%     (regenerate path).  The "Display" scenario itself does NOT
%%     re-run BookToIRS — it just serves whatever Form8825_FILL.pdf
%%     exists on disk.  Should the display path opportunistically
%%     regenerate when the FILL.pdf is older than the bookNS files?
%%     Currently: NO — operator must click Aid → Commit explicitly.
%%   • [Q2] /forms/<form_id>.pdf serves the binary directly via
%%     Flask send_file — no DB hit, no IRS-service hit.  This means
%%     a stale FILL.pdf on disk renders without warning even after
%%     bookNS edits.  Suggest: surface a "FILL.pdf is older than
%%     bookNS_*.json" badge on the IRS Tax view header.
%%   • [Q3] llcForm8825.stats() reads from stmtIncomeStmt to compute
%%     Gross Rents / Depreciation / Net.  Those numbers come from the
%%     ledger directly — they are NOT re-derived from the FILL.pdf.
%%     Possible drift if BookToIRS changes per-form aggregation rules.
%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as 'UI<br>Browser'
    participant JS as JavaScript (Frontend)
    participant API as Flask API (Routes)
    participant AM as ui.llcMgmt<br>(Middleware/Auth)
    participant UI as ui.llcForm8825<br>(View)
    participant Bk as ledger.stmtIncomeStmt<br>(BookSvc — stat chips only)
    participant IRS as irs.Form8825<br>(Form Processing)
    participant DB as DB_Json<br>(⛁ OBJs/Profile)
    participant BookNS as BookNS<br>(⛁ Namespace Control)
    participant FM as Form8825_FILL.pdf<br>(⛁ namespace/FILL)
    participant U as Util (Log/Help)
    participant H as Bookkeeper

    Note over B, U: Request Phase — start app & navigate
    B->>JS: User starts browser (URL=/)
    JS->>API: GET /
    API->>AM: dispatch (home route)
    AM->>UI: render_template("home.html", VIEW_GROUPS, eSession)
    UI-->>JS: HTML home page
    JS->>B: render Home (IRS Tax Aids group lists Form 8825)

    Note over B, U: User clicks Form 8825
    B->>JS: click /view/llcForm8825
    JS->>API: GET /view/llcForm8825
    API->>AM: dispatch view_object("llcForm8825")
    AM->>AM: _canonical_name("llcForm8825") → "llcForm8825"
    AM->>UI: manager = self.objects["llcForm8825"]
    AM->>AM: PDF_VIEWS lookup — skip load, render irs_pdf_view.html
    AM->>UI: manager.stats()
    UI->>Bk: stmtIncomeStmt(llc).load()
    Bk->>DB: read llcAssets / llcExpRev / llcPayables / llcReceivables
    DB-->>Bk: GL records
    Bk-->>UI: rows with acctType/acct/Balance
    UI->>UI: aggregate Gross Rents / Depreciation / Net Rental
    UI-->>AM: stats dict
    AM->>UI: manager.meta()
    UI->>UI: pdf_path() → Forms_IRS/Form8825_FILL.pdf  (existence check)
    UI-->>AM: meta dict (formId, pdfPath, pdfPresent, sources, note)
    AM->>AM: render_template("irs_pdf_view.html",<br>pdf_url="/forms/Form8825.pdf", stats, meta)
    AM-->>JS: HTML page (iframe src=/forms/Form8825.pdf)

    Note over B, U: Browser fetches the embedded PDF
    JS->>B: parse HTML — iframe issues GET request to /forms/Form8825.pdf
    B->>API: GET /forms/Form8825.pdf
    API->>AM: dispatch serve_irs_pdf("Form8825")
    AM->>AM: validate form_id in PDF_VIEWS
    AM->>FM: send_file(Forms_IRS/Form8825_FILL.pdf, mimetype=application/pdf)
    FM-->>AM: PDF bytes
    AM-->>JS: PDF stream

    Note over B, H: Response Phase — page + PDF rendered
    JS->>B: iframe renders Form8825_FILL.pdf
    JS->>B: stat chips (Gross Rents / Depreciation / Net Rental)
    JS->>B: 🛠 Aid button + inline modal partial loaded (hidden)

    %% Note: irs.Form8825, BookNS, and the Aid service are NOT touched
    %% in this scenario — they are loaded lazily only when the operator
    %% clicks the Aid button (see apiFlow_ChangeFieldMap_Form8825.mmdc).
